### 1. **Regular Pay**

Eliza works **40 hours** at her regular hourly rate of **$10/hour**.

$$
\text{Regular Pay} = 40 \times 10 = 400
$$

---

### 2. **Overtime Pay**

Eliza worked **45 hours total**, meaning she worked **5 hours of overtime** (since 45 - 40 = 5).

Overtime is paid at **1.2 times her regular rate**:

$$
\text{Overtime Rate} = 1.2 \times 10 = 12
$$

$$
\text{Overtime Pay} = 5 \times 12 = 60
$$

---

### 3. **Total Earnings**

$$
\text{Total Earnings} = \text{Regular Pay} + \text{Overtime Pay} = 400 + 60 = 460
$$

---

### Final Answer

$$
\boxed{460}
$$

