To calculate Jill's annual salary, we need to determine her weekly earnings from each job and then multiply by the number of weeks she works in a year.

---

### Step 1: Calculate weekly earnings from teaching

Jill works **35 hours per week** as a teacher and earns **$20 per hour**.

$$
\text{Weekly earnings from teaching} = 35 \text{ hours} \times 20 \text{ dollars/hour} = 700 \text{ dollars}
$$

---

### Step 2: Calculate weekly earnings from coaching

Jill works **15 hours per week** as a cheerleading coach and earns **$30 per hour**.

$$
\text{Weekly earnings from coaching} = 15 \text{ hours} \times 30 \text{ dollars/hour} = 450 \text{ dollars}
$$

---

### Step 3: Calculate total weekly earnings

$$
\text{Total weekly earnings} = 700 + 450 = 1150 \text{ dollars}
$$

---

### Step 4: Calculate annual salary

Jill works **50 weeks a year**.

$$
\text{Annual salary} = 1150 \text{ dollars/week} \times 50 \text{ weeks} = 57500 \text{ dollars}
$$

---

### Final Answer

$$
\boxed{57500}
$$

Jill's annual salary is **$57,500**. ✅

