   - To cover the remaining 6 miles in 1 hour, the required speed is:
     $$
     \text{Required speed} = \frac{\text{Remaining distance}}{\text{Remaining time}} = \frac{6}{1} = 6 \text{ miles per hour}.
     $$

Thus, Marissa needs to walk the remaining 6 miles at a speed of $\boxed{6}$ miles per hour to achieve an average speed of 4 miles per hour for the entire trail. 

