When a 25% discount is given on the original price, the new price is $ P - 0.25P = 0.75P $. According to the problem, after the discount, the price is $19.50. So we can set up the following equation:

$$ 0.75P = 19.50 $$

To find $ P $, we divide both sides of the equation by 0.75:

$$ P = \frac{19.50}{0.75} $$

Performing the division:

$$ P = 26 $$

Therefore, the original price of the book was $ \boxed{26} $ dollars.
