The problem involves calculating the total cost of ice cream that Cynthia will need to buy over a period of 60 days. Here's a step-by-step breakdown of the solution:

---

### Step 1: Determine Total Servings Needed
Cynthia eats **1 serving per night** for **60 days**, so:
$$
60 \text{ days} \times 1 \text{ serving/day} = 60 \text{ servings}
$$

---

### Step 2: Calculate Number of Cartons Required
Each carton contains **15 servings**. To find out how many cartons she needs:
$$
60 \text{ servings} \div 15 \text{ servings/carton} = 4 \text{ cartons}
$$

---

### Step 3: Calculate Total Cost
Each carton costs **$4.00**, so:
$$
4 \text{ cartons} \times 4 \text{ dollars/carton} = 16 \text{ dollars}
$$

---

