Jean starts with 30 lollipops. After eating 2, she has:

$$
30 - 2 = 28 \text{ lollipops remaining}
$$

She wants to pack these into bags, each containing 2 lollipops. To find out how many bags she can fill, divide the remaining lollipops by the number per bag:

$$
28 \div 2 = 14
$$

Thus, Jean can fill $\boxed{14}$ bags.  
