To determine how many bags of dog food Cscilia will use in the first year, we break the feeding schedule into two parts. For the first 180 days, the puppy is fed 1 cup per day, totaling $180 \times 1 = 180$ cups. For the remaining $365 - 180 = 185$ days, the puppy is fed 2 cups per day, totaling $185 \times 2 = 370$ cups. Adding these together gives $180 + 370 = 550$ cups needed for the year. Since each bag contains 110 cups, the total number of bags required is $\frac{550}{110} = 5$. 

\boxed{5} 
``` 

