Alternatively, maybe think in fractions. 2/3 of the girls are in the girl scout, so the remaining 1/3 are not. Therefore, 1/3 of 120. 120 divided by 3 is 40. So that's another way to see it. 

Therefore, the answer should be 40. 

I think that's solid. I don't see any errors in my reasoning. So the number of girls not in the girl scout is 40.

